🔥✌️How LLMs extract and understand brand entities and how you should create info about your business?👇

For a long time, natural language processing could only be used on a small scale. The Transformer technology invented by Google, which was rolled out on a large scale with BERT, makes NLP possible on a large scale.

BERT was also trained with structured data, which is used as human-labeled training data. Natural Language Processing itself does not need structured data such as schema markups to recognize and understand entities.

Modern language models are trained to understand unstructured natural language. Sentiment determination, named entity recognition, and entity extraction are part of NLP.

This is important to understand in order to position brands in a machine-understandable way within the context of brand context optimization.

Texts about brands should therefore always be created in such a way that the brand entities are the central focus and that topics and attributes are assigned to the brand entities using simple and clear sentence structures.

